From: SPIranha <https://github.com/MTSistemi/SPIranha>
Subject: [PATCH] reboot into BOOTSEL when opened at 1200 baud

Without this there is no way back into the ROM bootloader except pressing the
BOOTSEL button, which means a host tool can never update the programmer on its
own.

This is the Arduino Leonardo convention, and the same one pico_stdio_usb uses:
when the host sets the line coding to 1200 baud, the firmware calls
reset_usb_boot(). It cannot fire by accident - serprog hosts open the port at
their configured rate, typically 115200.

Verified on hardware: opening the port at 1200 baud makes the board come back
as the RPI-RP2 drive within a second.
---
diff --git a/main.c b/main.c
--- a/main.c
+++ b/main.c
@@ -14,6 +14,7 @@
 
 #include "pico/stdlib.h"
 #include "pico/binary_info.h"
+#include "pico/bootrom.h"
 #include "hardware/spi.h"
 #include "tusb.h"
 #include "serprog.h"
@@ -304,6 +305,20 @@ static void command_loop() {
 	}
 }
 
+/* Reboot into the ROM bootloader when the host opens the port at 1200 baud.
+ *
+ * This is the same convention as the Arduino Leonardo and pico_stdio_usb: it
+ * lets a host tool put the board back into BOOTSEL without anyone pressing the
+ * button. Nothing else uses 1200 baud - serprog hosts open the port at their
+ * configured rate, typically 115200 - so it cannot be triggered by accident.
+ */
+void tud_cdc_line_coding_cb(uint8_t itf, cdc_line_coding_t const *coding)
+{
+	(void)itf;
+	if (coding->bit_rate == 1200)
+		reset_usb_boot(0, 0);
+}
+
 int main() {
 	/* Metadata for picotool */
 	bi_decl(bi_program_description(DESCRIPTION));
